---
title: Tags
description: Browse every subject the writing touches.
permalink: /tags/
layout: blog-base.liquid
data:
  nav: tags
pagination:
  include: Tags
  per_page: 100
---
{% comment %}
  Tags — single-file pattern (designs 4a directory + 4b single-tag).

  Cobalt's `include: Tags` pagination generates BOTH from this one source:
    · the directory page  → /tags/index.html      (paginator.indexes is set)
    · one page per tag    → /tags/<tag>/index.html (paginator.pages is set)

  ⚠ Verified on Cobalt 0.20.2 (cc-prompt DD-2). Two facts drove this shape:
    1. `paginator.index_title` / `paginator.pages` do NOT exist on the directory
       page — only the LFE-style `paginator.indexes[]` (each with .index_title,
       .index_permalink, .total_pages, .pages) does. The two-file
       tags.liquid + tag.liquid design could not work; they are merged here.
    2. `sub.index_permalink` renders as `tags//<tag>` (double slash, no leading
       slash). The generated FILE is at /tags/<tag>/, matching the tag chips, so
       we build the href from `sub.index_title` — never from index_permalink.
{% endcomment %}
{% if paginator.indexes %}
{% comment %} ── Directory page (design 4a) ──
   NB: `collections` is NOT in scope on paginated pages (verified 0.20.2), so the
   distinct article count isn't computable here — the eyebrow shows tag count only. {% endcomment %}
<header style="padding-block-start: var(--space-2xl);">
  <p class="blog-eyebrow">{{ paginator.indexes.size }} tags</p>
  <h1 class="article-title" style="max-inline-size: none; margin-block-start: var(--space-s);">Tags</h1>
  <p class="featured__dek">Every subject the writing touches, with a count of how often. The recurring ones are the through-line.</p>
</header>

<div class="tag-directory" style="margin-block-start: var(--space-l);">
{% for sub in paginator.indexes %}
  {% assign c = sub.total_pages %}
  {% assign size_class = "" %}
  {% if c >= 5 %}{% assign size_class = "is-xl" %}{% elsif c >= 3 %}{% assign size_class = "is-l" %}{% elsif c <= 1 %}{% assign size_class = "is-s" %}{% endif %}
  <div class="tag-directory__row {{ size_class }}">
    <a href="/tags/{{ sub.index_title }}/" class="tag-directory__name">#{{ sub.index_title }}</a>
    <span class="tag-directory__lead"></span>
    <span class="tag-directory__count">{{ c }}</span>
  </div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

{% else %}
{% comment %} ── Single-tag page (design 4b) ── {% endcomment %}
{% assign tag = paginator.index_title %}

<a href="/tags/" class="article-back" style="margin-block-start: var(--space-2xl);">&larr; All tags</a>

<div class="tag-hero" style="margin-block-start: var(--space-m);">
  <h1 class="tag-hero__name">#{{ tag }}</h1>
  <span class="tag-hero__count">{{ paginator.pages.size }} articles</span>
</div>

<hr class="rule-strong" style="margin-block-start: var(--space-l);">

<ul class="post-list">
  {% for post in paginator.pages %}
  <li class="post-entry">
    <div class="article-meta">
      <span>{{ post.published_date | date: "%b %d, %Y" }}</span><span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <span>{{ post.data.minutes }} min</span>
    </div>
    <a href="/{{ post.permalink }}" class="post-entry__title">{{ post.title }}</a>
    {% if post.description %}<p class="post-entry__dek">{{ post.description }}</p>{% endif %}
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
